{%- comment -%}
  Price drop — the discount, stated once, computed from the product.

  ZERO MAINTENANCE IS THE WHOLE DESIGN. Nothing here is typed: not the price, not the old
  price, not the percentage, not the saving. Every number is read from the product at
  render time, so putting the price back up needs no edit anywhere. The moment
  compare-at stops being higher than price — because the price went up, or because the
  compare-at was cleared — this block renders nothing at all and vanishes from the page.
  A sale badge that has to be remembered is a sale badge that eventually lies.

  THE LINE MUST NOT CONTAIN A PRICE. It is the one field a human writes, and the
  temptation is to put the figures in it — "back to $29.99 soon". Do that and the whole
  design is undone: the block keeps its numbers current automatically and that sentence
  does not, so the day the price moves the page contradicts itself. Say why, and say that
  it ends. Let the computed parts say how much.

  IT FAILS CLOSED. If an end date is set and that date has passed, the block stops
  rendering rather than quietly carrying on. The classic dark pattern is the offer that
  keeps announcing itself after it ended, or the timer that resets on refresh; the only
  way to be sure this never does either is to make expiry mean disappear.

  WHAT IT DELIBERATELY IS NOT. No stock counter — the product is a file, there is no
  scarcity and claiming one would be a lie. No ticking clock. This shop sells to people
  whose condition runs on urgency and doubt, and a countdown works by manufacturing
  exactly the pressure these workbooks exist to unwind. A real deadline stated as a date
  is honest and does the same job; a clock counting down milliseconds is theatre aimed at
  the nervous system.

  PROOF INSTEAD OF EXPLANATION. A large unexplained discount can read as "this is what it
  is worth" rather than "this is a bargain", and at ninety per cent off that risk is real.
  But the fix is not to explain the price by confessing. Copy in the shape of "we are new"
  tells a stranger you have no track record and no reason to be chosen over anyone else,
  which costs more trust than the discount ever did. So this line carries evidence other
  people have already bought, and lets the buyer draw their own conclusion about why it is
  cheap. If the price ever does need explaining outright, set an end date instead: the
  block then states what the price returns to and when, in the flattest possible register.
  That is a reason without an apology.

  "RECENTLY" IS THE ONE WORD HERE THAT CAN GO STALE. The count cannot — the plus sees to
  that. But a claim that sales happened recently stops being true if sales stop, and no
  code can notice. It is true at the time of writing by a wide margin. If the shop ever
  goes quiet for a long stretch, drop the word rather than the number.

  THE GLOW IS LIT, NOT FLASHING. It does not pulse, fade in, or breathe. A highlight that
  moves keeps reclaiming the eye, which is the countdown trick in a nicer outfit, and this
  shop sells to people for whom that is the symptom. A static glow says "read this" once
  and then holds still. It also costs nothing: no animation frame, no repaint, no script.

  YELLOW BECAUSE IT IS NOT THE BUTTON. The accent green is what the customer clicks; if
  the one sentence asking to be read wore it too, the page would have two greens competing
  and only one of them would do anything. The yellow is the palette's own foreground hue
  at full saturation, so it belongs to the site without ever being mistaken for a control.

  THE SOLD COUNT IS A TOKEN, NOT A TYPED NUMBER. Write [sold] in the reason and the figure
  comes from its own setting, so raising it later is editing one field rather than
  rewriting a sentence — the same reason the overlap messages use [items] and [bundle].
  Always follow it with a plus. A figure with a plus after it can only ever become an
  understatement as sales accumulate; a bare figure becomes wrong the next time someone
  buys. Round down for the same reason. This is the one number in the block that is not
  computed, and the plus is what keeps it from going stale the way a typed price would.

  AND IT FAILS CLOSED LIKE EVERYTHING ELSE. If the reason asks for [sold] and no count has
  been set, the reason line does not render at all. A half-substituted sentence reading
  "+ sold across Etsy and here" is worse than no sentence.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign product = closest.product
  assign price = product.price
  assign was = product.compare_at_price

  assign on_sale = false
  if was > price and price > 0
    assign on_sale = true
  endif

  comment
    An end date that has passed takes the whole block down with it. Compared at the end
    of the named day, in the shop's timezone, so "ends the 30th" includes the 30th.
  endcomment
  assign expired = false
  if block.settings.ends_at != blank
    assign now_stamp = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    assign end_stamp = block.settings.ends_at | date: '%s' | plus: 86399
    if now_stamp > end_stamp
      assign expired = true
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- if on_sale and expired == false -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign saved = was | minus: price
    assign percent = saved | times: 100.0 | divided_by: was | round
    assign accent = block.settings.accent | default: '#39FF14'
    assign glow = block.settings.glow_color | default: '#FFCF3D'
    assign glow_near = glow | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.32
    assign glow_far = glow | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.15

    assign reason = block.settings.reason
    assign sold = block.settings.sold_count | strip
    assign reason_ok = true
    if reason contains '[sold]'
      if sold == blank
        assign reason_ok = false
      else
        assign reason = reason | replace: '[sold]', sold
      endif
    endif
  -%}

  <div
    class="pdr"
    style="--pdr-accent:{{ accent }};--pdr-glow:{{ glow }};--pdr-glow-near:{{ glow_near }};--pdr-glow-far:{{ glow_far }};"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    <p class="pdr__row">
      {%- if block.settings.show_percent -%}
        <span class="pdr__pill">{{ percent }}% off</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      <span class="pdr__saved">You save {{ saved | money }}</span>
    </p>

    {%- if reason != blank and reason_ok -%}
      <p class="pdr__reason{% if block.settings.reason_glow %} pdr__reason--glow{% endif %}">
        {{- reason | escape -}}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if block.settings.ends_at != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Only claim a deadline when there is one. The date and the old price are both read
        from live data, so neither can drift out of step with what is actually charged.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="pdr__ends">
        Back to {{ was | money }} after {{ block.settings.ends_at | date: '%-d %B' }}.
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- style -%}
    .pdr { margin: 2px 0 0; color: inherit; }

    .pdr__row {
      margin: 0;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    /* The one loud element on the page, and it is loud because it is true. */
    .pdr__pill {
      background: var(--pdr-accent);
      color: #0B0F0D;
      font-size: .68rem;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: .07em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      padding: 3px 9px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .pdr__saved {
      font-size: .82rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    }

    .pdr__reason { margin: 6px 0 0; font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.45; opacity: .78; }

    /* Weight 500 on purpose: the theme loads Inter 400/500/700, and a glow hung on
       hairline text reads as blur rather than light. Full opacity for the same reason. */
    .pdr__reason--glow {
      opacity: 1;
      color: var(--pdr-glow);
      font-size: .84rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      text-shadow:
        0 0 10px var(--pdr-glow-near),
        0 0 26px var(--pdr-glow-far);
    }

    /* Anyone who has asked for more contrast wants the letterforms, not the halo. */
    @media (prefers-contrast: more) {
      .pdr__reason--glow { text-shadow: none; }
    }

    .pdr__ends { margin: 3px 0 0; font-size: .76rem; line-height: 1.45; opacity: .6; }
  {%- endstyle -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Price drop",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Reads the product's price and compare-at price. Every number is computed, so nothing here needs editing when the price changes — and the block disappears on its own the moment the product is no longer discounted."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "reason",
      "label": "The line under the price",
      "default": "[sold]+ sold recently!",
      "info": "The only line a human writes. Write [sold] where the number goes. Keep prices OUT of it — the figures above update themselves, this sentence would not. Naming a channel or a timeframe only invites the reader to audit the claim; the bare number reads as bigger than whatever they would have checked."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "sold_count",
      "label": "Copies sold recently (all channels)",
      "default": "21",
      "info": "Just the digits — the copy supplies the plus. Round DOWN. A number with a plus after it only ever becomes an understatement as sales come in, so this never needs updating on a schedule. Leave it empty and the reason line stops showing rather than printing a gap."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "reason_glow",
      "label": "Glow the reason line",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Lights the sentence so it is read instead of skimmed past. It does not blink or pulse."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "glow_color",
      "label": "Glow colour",
      "default": "#FFCF3D",
      "info": "The site's own warm off-white at full saturation. Keep it different from the button colour — yellow marks the line as worth reading, green means clickable."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "ends_at",
      "label": "Last day of the offer",
      "info": "YYYY-MM-DD. Optional. Leave empty for no deadline. If the date passes, the whole block stops showing rather than claiming an offer that has ended."
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_percent", "label": "Show the percentage", "default": true },
    { "type": "color", "id": "accent", "label": "Accent colour", "default": "#39FF14" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Price drop" }]
}
{% endschema %}
